v0.6 picks JSONL (newline-delimited JSON, one MemoryRecord per line) as the export format, NOT `.sql` dump or Parquet. Why:
(a) grep-friendly — `grep '"kind":"lesson"' export.jsonl` works;
(b) diff-friendly — git/code-review tools handle line-oriented well;
(c) append-able — future memory_export --append is a one-line change;
(d) schema-evolution friendly — each line is self-describing, so v0.7 adding a field doesn't break v0.6 importers (they ignore unknown), and v0.7 importers can fill defaults for missing fields.
Tradeoff vs Parquet: ~3× larger on disk (text vs columnar). Acceptable at memory-data sizes (few thousand rows max).
